      "role": "user",
      "content": "the \"industry standard\" part is a bit vague though. like, when people talk about \"harmful political opinion\" vs actual satire, there's a huge debate about it. some platforms are way stricter about protecting certain groups even if the post is \"satire,\" while others say that's just censorship. in your view, should we be prioritizing the prevention of social harm or the protection of edgy political speech? which one is the more \"standard\" approach for a modern platform?",
