      "content": "There isn't a single universal \"standard\" as major platforms often explicitly state on their own policies that prioritizing the prevention of severe social harm takes precedence over the protection of controversial political speech. While some approach this more aggressively to combat harassment and misinformation, the dominant trend in modern content moderation is a harm-based framework rather than a blanket censorship of edgy views. For a new launch, adopting the \"most serious harm\" threshold—satire that is not just offensive but incites violence or targets protected groups—is currently the most legally defensible and scalable path.",
