      "content": "ok but \"the dominant trend\" and \"most legally defensible\" sounds like you're saying we should definitely go with the harm-based approach. isn't that basically saying we should prioritize deplatforming people who use satire to mock certain political ideologies? it feels like if we follow that \"standard,\" we're just building a platform that's inherently biased against anyone who isn't part of the mainstream consensus. isn't there a risk that the \"harm-based\" model is just a way to label any uncomfortable political speech as \"harmful\"?",
